End the session when the host goes silent.

Nothing noticed a host that simply stopped sending: a Steam Deck put to sleep mid-stream left
the session connected forever, with the last picture on screen. A connected host sends video,
audio and stats all the time, so the session now notes when the last packet arrived, and a
one-second timer task disconnects it after 10 s without one. IHS_SessionStreamStats.timedOut
tells the app it ended that way rather than by request (the host's own Disconnect packet
still ends it as before). The task runs while the session worker does and is stopped
synchronously in SessionFinalized; it never ends by itself, so that stop can't hit a task
already freed.

